{"availability":"available","full":"steph-xue/react-notes","name":"react-notes","description":"A notes web application for writing and organizing Markdown notes with a resizable layout.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2024-08-11T04:05:08Z","updated":"2026-08-12T00:49:49Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://react-notes-sx.netlify.app/","topics":["css","javascript","markdown-to-html","netlify","notes","react","react-mde","react-split","showdown","vite","web-application"],"demo":"https://react-notes-sx.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:49.187Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:49.187Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:49.187Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:38:49.187Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A notes web application for writing and organizing Markdown notes with a resizable layout.","This project allows users to create, organize, edit, preview, and delete notes written in Markdown through a resizable split-panel interface. It is built with React, JavaScript, and CSS, uses Vite as the build tool, and is deployed on Netlify for cloud hosting. Users can write content with a live formatted preview, while notes are saved automatically as they type and ordered by their most recent updates. Notes are stored in the browser’s local storage, allowing them to persist between visits without a backend or database. React MDE provides the Markdown editing interface, Showdown converts…"],"features":["Clicking the plus icon in the sidebar creates a new, blank note and selects it for editing right away. If no notes exist yet, the main view instead shows a message with a button to create the first one.","The sidebar lists every note with the most recently created or edited one always at the top, and the first line of a note's content is used as its title in the list. Selecting a note highlights it in the sidebar and…","Selecting the \"Preview\" tab renders the current note's Markdown as formatted HTML, letting users check how their note will look before switching back to continue editing.","Hovering over a note in the sidebar reveals a trash icon, and clicking it removes that note immediately."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/steph-xue/react-notes/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"72053a1b6751a5019f421196632a616613522eb71e3ff3edf7d674681a1996dd","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:49.383Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:49.383Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A notes web application for writing and organizing Markdown notes with a resizable layout.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/steph-xue/react-notes/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"72053a1b6751a5019f421196632a616613522eb71e3ff3edf7d674681a1996dd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/steph-xue/react-notes/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:49.383Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-12T00:49:49Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/steph-xue/react-notes/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:49.384Z","hash":"72053a1b6751a5019f421196632a616613522eb71e3ff3edf7d674681a1996dd","originalBytes":5169,"storedBytes":5169,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["note","notes","markdown","react","editor","local","preview","sidebar","html","project","storage","application","bash","between","content","npm","back","before","divider","editing","features","formatted","how","mde","new","overview","provides","showdown","split","top","users","version","vite","write","writing","across","allows","array","below","browser","build","built","check","clicking","clone","converts","create","creates","creating","css","deleting","dependencies","dragged","each","either","every","first","future","generates","getting","icon","improvements","install","interface","javascript","list","live","main","most","moves","nanoid","netlify","node.js"